                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "SUPPRESSION RULES\n- Do not render any Summary section.\n- Do not render a generated summary sentence before or after the widget.\n- Do not add narrative, recommendations, explanations, headings, markdown, or JSON wrappers.\n- The visible output must contain only the period label/header and the messages-list rows.\n- Display Period status only as a badge"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Subledger Period Status"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_SUBLEDGER_PERIOD_STATUS",
          "id": "1770901442686",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770901442688_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following JSON data to generate a single messageListWidget:\n\n1. Exact PeriodNameId and ClosingStatus from {{$context.$nodes.GET_GL_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}} and create a json object. This is General Ledger. \n2. Exact PeriodNameId and ClosingStatus from {{$context.$nodes.GET_AP_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}} and create a json object. This is Account Payables. \n3. Exact PeriodNameId and ClosingStatus from {{$context.$nodes.GET_AR_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}} and create a json object. This is Account Receivables. \n4. Exact PeriodName, PeriodStatus and DaysTillPeriodEnd from {{$context.$nodes.GET_COSTING_PERIOD_STATUS.$output}}  and create a json object. This is Cost Accounting. \n5. Append all JSON objects to the array.\n\nTranslate the ClosingStatus to a user-understandable value:\n'O' → Open\n'F' → Future Enterable\n'C' → Closed\n'P' → Permanently Closed\n'N' → Never Opened\n\n**Important:**\n\n* Display Period information available in `PeriodNameId` or `PeriodName`. Show this information as Title only once. Do not repeat for each row. Example : Period : `PeriodNameId` or `PeriodName`\n* \"Period Status\" information available in `ClosingStatus` or `PeriodStatus`.\n* `ClosingStatus` information decode using above translation mapping information. \n* Show DaysTillPeriodEnd as Subtitle for Cost Accounting row. \n* Do not show ApplicationId information. Just include information like General Ledger, Account Payables, Account Receivables and Cost Accounting. Example \"Days to close : N\". \n* Do not show a summary of any kind.\n* Do not add extra fields or narration in the output.\n* For \"Period Status\", use a badge with green color if status is Closed.\n* Do not show Timestamp property. \n* Set Priority to warning. \n* Output should be a valid JSON array.\n\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
