              "value": "Generate `ora.Agent(\"CLOSE_PERIOD\")` and set actionText property as \"Close Period\". Set the priority value as true and title property value as \"Cost Accounting Period Close Period\"."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format User Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_USER_QUERY",
          "id": "1770903114093",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770903114095_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Read period status details from the following sources based on `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`:\n\n* General Ledger → `{{$context.$nodes.GET_GL_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}}`\n* Accounts Payable → `{{$context.$nodes.GET_AP_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}}`\n* Accounts Receivable → `{{$context.$nodes.GET_AR_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}}`\n\nTranslate each `ClosingStatus` code to a user-friendly description:\n\n* `'O'` → **Open**\n* `'F'` → **Future Enterable**\n* `'C'` → **Closed**\n* `'P'` → **Permanently Closed**\n* `'N'` → **Never Opened**\n\nDetermine the overall period readiness:\n\n* If **any** of the three modules (GL, AP, AR) has status **Open**, then the period is **not ready for closure**.\n* Only use the `applicationId` and `PeriodStatus` values internally for interpretation — **never display them** in the response.\n\nOutput a **clear and concise summary** indicating whether the period is ready to close, and mention which subledgers are still open if applicable.\n\nSummarize the output in a concise, bulleted list that highlights the key insights relevant to the user’s query. Ensure the response focuses solely on the available data and does not include raw data or field names. Do not introduce any additional information; only present what is directly available."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fill Parameters"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FILL_PARAMETERS",
          "id": "1771632686365",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771632686366_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use data from \n1. Exact PeriodNameId and ClosingStatus from {{$context.$nodes.GET_GL_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}} and create a json object. This is General Ledger. \n2. Exact PeriodNameId and ClosingStatus from {{$context.$nodes.GET_AP_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}} and create a json object. This is Account Payables. \n3. Exact PeriodNameId and ClosingStatus from {{$context.$nodes.GET_AR_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}} and create a json object. This is Account Receivables. \n4. Exact PeriodName, PeriodStatus and DaysTillPeriodEnd from {{$context.$nodes.GET_COSTING_PERIOD_STATUS.$output}}  and create a json object. This is Cost Accounting. \n\nTranslate the ClosingStatus to a user-understandable value:\n'O' → Open\n'F' → Future Enterable\n'C' → Closed\n'P' → Permanently Closed\n'N' → Never Opened\n\nFill parameters in {{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check Period Is Open and Last Week",
            "returnType": "boolean",
            "sourceCode": "const start = new Date($context.$variables.periodStartDate); \nconst end = new Date($context.$variables.periodEndDate); \nconst current = new Date($context.$system.$currentDate);\nconst periodStatus = $context.$variables.periodStatusCode;\n//const current = new Date(\"2026-05-28\");\n//const periodStatus = \"C\";\n\nif (isNaN(start.getTime()) || isNaN(current.getTime())) {\n  return false;\n}\n\nstart.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);\nend.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);\ncurrent.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);\n\nconst daysDifference =\n  (current.getTime() - start.getTime()) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24);\n\nreturn (\n  periodStatus === \"O\" &&\n  ((daysDifference >= 21 && daysDifference <= 34) || (end.getTime() < current.getTime()))\n);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777529734355"
          },
          "code": "CHECK_PERIOD_IS_OPEN_AND_LAST_WEEK",
          "id": "1777529541776",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is Period Open Or In Last Week"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1777529854197",
            "false": "1777529814965"
          },
          "code": "IS_PERIOD_OPEN_OR_IN_LAST_WEEK",
