          },
          "code": "RETURN_JUST_EMPTY_STRING",
          "id": "1777529814965",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777529814966_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Return exactly:\n\n`\"\"`\n\nDo not include any other text, whitespace, or formatting."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Subledger Status Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUBLEDGER_STATUS_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1777529854197",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777529854198_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given period close status information for multiple subledgers. Subledger status is critical during period close because all relevant subledgers should ideally be closed before completing close activities.\n\nUsing only the data from the objects below, generate a concise 1-2 sentence business summary for a Cost Accountant user persona.\n\nINPUT SOURCES AND REQUIRED FIELDS\nExtract only the exact fields listed below and internally structure them as JSON objects before generating the summary. Do not output the intermediate JSON.\n\n1. General Ledger\n   Source: {{$context.$nodes.GET_GL_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}}\n   Fields: PeriodNameId, ClosingStatus\n\n2. Accounts Payable\n   Source: {{$context.$nodes.GET_AP_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}}\n   Fields: PeriodNameId, ClosingStatus\n\n3. Accounts Receivable\n   Source: {{$context.$nodes.GET_AR_SUBLEDGER_STATUS.$output}}\n   Fields: PeriodNameId, ClosingStatus\n\n4. Cost Accounting\n   Source: {{$context.$nodes.GET_COSTING_PERIOD_STATUS.$output}}\n   Fields: PeriodName, PeriodStatus, DaysTillPeriodEnd\n\nSUMMARY REQUIREMENTS\n- Return only the final business summary in 1-2 concise sentences.\n- Use only information present in the provided objects.\n- Highlight whether any subledgers are still open, not closed, or otherwise not in a closed status.\n- Include the Cost Accounting period status when available.\n- Include DaysTillPeriodEnd when available.\n\nDAY COUNT INTERPRETATION\nWhen referencing DaysTillPeriodEnd:\n- If the value is negative, state that the period is overdue by the absolute value of that number of days.\n- If the value is positive, state that there are that many days left to close the period.\n- If the value is zero, state that the period is due today.\n\nOUTPUT RULES\n- Do not include intermediate JSON objects.\n- Do not add commentary, explanations, assumptions, or information not present in the objects.\n- If all input objects are empty, null, undefined, or contain no meaningful data, return an empty response."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
